                  "content": "SELECTED: candidate_12\n\nCONFIDENCE: HIGH\n\nEXPLANATION:\nThe fix commit (fix_commit_diff.txt) modifies the single-selection branch of\nSavedHqlExportToCSV.export() by wrapping the existing logic in \"if (value != null) { ... }\".\nBefore the fix, the code was:\n\n    String value = helper.getParameter(option.name());\n    SavedHQLInterface.IdValue v = new SavedHQLInterface.IdValue();\n    v.setValue(option.name());\n    Long id = option.lookupValue(context.getUser(), value);\n    if (id == null) {\n        try { id = Long.valueOf(value); } catch (NumberFormatException e) {}\n    }\n    v.setText(id == null ? \"\" : id.toString());\n    params.add(v);\n\nThis is exactly the buggy pattern: when a single-choice parameter such as SUBJECT or\nDEPARTMENT is not supplied by the request (helper.getParameter(option.name()) returns\nnull), the code still unconditionally calls option.lookupValue(user, null), which (for\nimplementations like DEPARTMENT/SUBJECT that call value.equalsIgnoreCase(...)) throws a\nNullPointerException, breaking the CSV export.\n\nSearching all 14 candidates for this exact block, candidate_12 is the commit that FIRST\nintroduces it. Candidate_12 is a large refactor of SavedHqlExportToCSV.java that replaces\nthe old positional-parameter export logic with the new per-Option loop:\n\n    for (SavedHQL.Option option: SavedHQL.Option.values()) {\n        ...\n        } else {\n            String value = helper.getParameter(option.name());\n            SavedHQLInterface.IdValue v = new SavedHQLInterface.IdValue();\n            v.setValue(option.name());\n            Long id = option.lookupValue(context.getUser(), value);\n            if (id == null) {\n                try { id = Long.valueOf(value); } catch (NumberFormatException e) {}\n            }\n            v.setText(id == null ? \"\" : id.toString());\n            params.add(v);\n        }\n    }\n\nThis is byte-for-byte identical (modulo formatting) to the pre-fix code shown in\nfix_commit_diff.txt, with no null-check on `value`. Candidate_12 also adds the\n`lookupValue` implementations (e.g. DEPARTMENT: `value.equalsIgnoreCase(d.getDeptCode())`,\nSUBJECT: `value.equalsIgnoreCase(s.getSubjectAreaAbbreviation())`), confirming that calling\nthese with a null `value` would throw an NPE \u2014 precisely the failure the fix commit\naddresses.\n\nEarlier candidates (candidate_01, candidate_05) only contain the older positional-index\nbased parameter logic (`v.setText(i < p.length ? p[i] : \"\")`) and do not yet have the\n`option.lookupValue(context.getUser(), value)` call at all, so the bug did not exist in\nthose versions. Later candidate_13 adds unrelated SavedHQLParameter handling but leaves\nthis single-selection block untouched, and candidate_14 is the actual fix commit (it\nmatches fix_commit_diff.txt exactly), so it cannot be the introducing commit. This\nconfirms candidate_12 is the commit that introduced the bug.\n"
                }
